n to the cloud volume to  do this I'm using IBM aspera on cloud  once uploaded I can move this footage  into my cloud volume I could also use  other industry standard file transfer  tools such as Cygnet or even drive file  stream for ingesting footage I'm going  to add this footage to my edit and drop  it into the timeline then I'm going to  pass the modified project over to  another editor let's bring in my  colleague Marku a Solutions Architect  who is based in Tokyo he's going to make  some additional changes to this edit  then send it back to me for rendering  hey thanks Adrian ok on my cloud  workstation I can see it the edits that  you made I can see the exact same  project data because we are using an  edible Obul file cast and when I open  the set Premiere Pro project any assets  of files that changed will be read  across  cause network and cast locally to the  Tokyo region I'm going to add my own  footage from the game using the same  technique that Adrienne did  and once this footage is available I  will add it to the Edit I save my  changes to the team project and now  Adrienne users get a notification thanks  mark ooh I see those changes almost  immediately on my workstation and the  footage you uploaded is coming across  now  all right thanks Adrienne see you later  I could render this edit on my virtual  workstation on a separate server running  Adobe Media encoder or using any one of  our partner transcoding solutions on  Google Cloud for this project I'm  rendering the video on another instance  when the render is done I can view the  result on my virtual workstation and  play back the videos I generated at full  resolution this is a relatively simple  example of a virtual post-production  suite we didn't cover asset ingestion or  archive and disaster recovery we also  didn't explore how intelligent content  discovery can help content creators  understand organize and monetize their  assets on Google cloud this demo showed  you connecting to and perf